WEBVTT

00:00:05.068 --> 00:00:07.362
You're an actor, aren't you?

00:00:07.445 --> 00:00:09.239
I'm the actor and performer,

00:00:09.322 --> 00:00:11.783
Konta Hoshino.

00:00:11.866 --> 00:00:15.328
I heard from Midori
that you're mainly working as an extra.

00:00:15.411 --> 00:00:19.249
Well, extras live as the character too,
so they are actors. Just so you know.

00:00:19.332 --> 00:00:22.085
You were just lazing around
at our parents' house.

00:00:22.168 --> 00:00:24.462
The three of us
actually post videos online.

00:00:24.546 --> 00:00:26.756
Would you consider appearing in one?

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.258
Hey.

00:00:28.341 --> 00:00:30.385
This guy is an actor.

00:00:30.468 --> 00:00:32.137
Oh, the video from the other day?

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.346
They actually uploaded it.

00:00:33.429 --> 00:00:34.931
Hey, look at the channel name.

00:00:35.014 --> 00:00:37.016
"The Empty Boys: We're Gonna Smash It!"

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.228
I stumbled on it while looking
at a channel run by my college friends!

00:00:40.311 --> 00:00:42.021
This guy isn't bad…

00:00:42.814 --> 00:00:45.942
You know, he might actually
be pretty interesting.

00:00:46.025 --> 00:00:48.027
WE SPOKE TO SUCCESSFUL BUSINESSMAN
KONTA HOSHINO!

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:54.075
What? I didn't get picked?

00:00:54.159 --> 00:00:55.910
You didn't. Too bad.

00:00:55.994 --> 00:01:00.373
But wasn't the role mine already,
and the audition was just a formality?

00:01:00.456 --> 00:01:02.125
That's what I heard.

00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:05.545
But Konta, you added your own lines
in the audition without permission.

00:01:05.628 --> 00:01:07.797
What? Right, I did do that.

00:01:07.881 --> 00:01:10.967
You turned two lines of dialogue
into about eight lines?

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:14.137
Oh, eight lines?
Did I talk that much? Yeah…

00:01:14.721 --> 00:01:16.556
That's why you didn't get picked!

00:01:16.639 --> 00:01:17.682
What?

00:01:17.765 --> 00:01:21.436
I was acting straight from the soul,
and I just happened to speak eight lines!

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.938
Listen here, Konta.

00:01:24.022 --> 00:01:28.735
An audition is where you show what you've
got, with the few lines you're given!

00:01:28.818 --> 00:01:31.487
The heck is that?

00:01:32.488 --> 00:01:34.782
And I was so confident about it too.

00:01:43.416 --> 00:01:45.668
Konta, what's for dinner toni--

00:01:48.171 --> 00:01:49.214
What's wrong?

00:01:55.845 --> 00:01:58.389
Konta seems kind of depressed.

00:01:59.015 --> 00:02:01.768
The slumped back of an unemployed man.

00:02:02.393 --> 00:02:03.770
Oh, wait, we're unemployed too.

00:02:04.646 --> 00:02:06.648
Is he going to be okay?

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:17.784
Hey, did something happen to Konta?

00:02:17.867 --> 00:02:20.328
He's over there alone, looking all sad.

00:02:21.704 --> 00:02:22.872
I knew it.

00:02:22.956 --> 00:02:24.415
Huh? What do you mean?

00:02:24.499 --> 00:02:27.543
I bet he failed another audition.

00:02:28.711 --> 00:02:31.881
Whenever he fails an audition,
he listens to Fun-Mon.

00:02:31.965 --> 00:02:33.216
Funky Monkey Babys?

00:02:33.299 --> 00:02:35.927
Yeah. Apparently,
it helps him feel better.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:40.014
But is he really all right?
From behind, he looks totally defeated.

00:02:40.098 --> 00:02:41.557
Well, he'll be fine.

00:02:41.641 --> 00:02:43.476
He'll be back to usual soon enough.

00:02:44.102 --> 00:02:46.479
-The power of Fun-Mon is amazing.
-Right?

00:02:55.071 --> 00:02:56.406
What?

00:02:56.489 --> 00:02:58.449
Am I getting scolded again?

00:02:58.533 --> 00:03:01.160
MANAGER

00:03:03.121 --> 00:03:04.414
Yes, hello?

00:03:05.748 --> 00:03:06.791
What?

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:08.876
A documentary?

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.255
On me?

00:03:50.126 --> 00:03:51.711
He's back.

00:03:51.794 --> 00:03:54.255
Konta, we started eating dinner.

00:03:59.052 --> 00:04:00.470
Want some beer?

00:04:00.553 --> 00:04:01.763
No, I'm good.

00:04:02.638 --> 00:04:03.848
I'll have barley tea.

00:04:05.975 --> 00:04:07.810
Isn't he kind of gloomy?

00:04:07.894 --> 00:04:09.562
Did Fun-Mon have no effect?

00:04:36.339 --> 00:04:37.590
Thanks for the food.

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:52.021
Hey.

00:04:54.565 --> 00:04:57.402
Do you know a show called
Document Memoreal?

00:05:00.279 --> 00:05:01.697
Huh? Yeah.

00:05:01.781 --> 00:05:03.116
I know it.

00:05:03.199 --> 00:05:05.159
It's that famous
day-in-the-life show, right?

00:05:05.243 --> 00:05:06.244
Yeah.

00:05:07.245 --> 00:05:11.707
That show called and said
they want to do a feature on me.

00:05:12.291 --> 00:05:13.793
Say what?

00:05:13.876 --> 00:05:15.128
Yeah.

00:05:15.211 --> 00:05:17.588
Come on, what a lame lie.

00:05:17.672 --> 00:05:18.965
No, I'm serious.

00:05:19.048 --> 00:05:21.759
No, there's no way that's true! Right?

00:05:22.969 --> 00:05:24.137
You're being tricked.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:27.014
No, really. My manager
just called me a moment ago.

00:05:27.098 --> 00:05:29.183
He said they want to film
my life as an actor.

00:05:29.267 --> 00:05:31.561
Wait, seriously? Why?

00:05:31.644 --> 00:05:33.479
Is it really that unbelievable?

00:05:33.563 --> 00:05:35.481
Yeah, I mean, you aren't successful.

00:05:35.565 --> 00:05:37.567
Your fame as an actor is basically zero.

00:05:38.776 --> 00:05:42.488
Why did they even have the idea
to make you an offer in the first place?

00:05:42.572 --> 00:05:46.325
Apparently, their staff
saw the video those boys made

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:49.078
the other day.

00:05:49.162 --> 00:05:51.372
-Huh?
-The video?

00:05:52.832 --> 00:05:53.666
This one?

00:05:53.749 --> 00:05:55.001
Yes, that one.

00:05:55.084 --> 00:05:58.880
Supposedly, the name "Empty Boys"
caught on, and it went a bit viral.

00:05:59.964 --> 00:06:02.925
Wait. So they saw this and made an offer?

00:06:03.009 --> 00:06:03.885
Yes.

00:06:04.635 --> 00:06:06.429
What a strange world.

00:06:06.512 --> 00:06:07.597
Wait.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:09.849
But if it's true, isn't this amazing?

00:06:09.932 --> 00:06:13.311
I'm telling you, it's true.
They saw this and sent me an offer!

00:06:13.394 --> 00:06:14.854
No way!

00:06:14.937 --> 00:06:16.230
That's awesome!

00:06:16.314 --> 00:06:18.149
He'll be a documentary actor.

00:06:18.232 --> 00:06:19.650
You did it!

00:06:19.734 --> 00:06:21.903
I guess so, but…

00:06:22.486 --> 00:06:23.321
What?

00:06:24.405 --> 00:06:27.158
What's with that attitude?

00:06:27.241 --> 00:06:29.327
Well, you see, I'm thinking

00:06:30.244 --> 00:06:31.787
maybe I'll turn it down.

00:06:32.496 --> 00:06:33.664
Seriously?

00:06:33.748 --> 00:06:35.833
Why?! This is a huge opportunity!

00:06:35.917 --> 00:06:37.460
It is, but…

00:06:37.543 --> 00:06:39.337
What? What is it?

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:44.300
Listen, a day-in-the-life feature means
they'll film my private life, right?

00:06:44.383 --> 00:06:45.927
Well, of course they will.

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:48.804
How is that going to turn out?

00:06:48.888 --> 00:06:50.348
Huh? Is there a problem?

00:06:50.431 --> 00:06:51.974
There is!

00:06:52.058 --> 00:06:55.436
Actors are supposed to keep
their private lives a mystery!

00:06:56.187 --> 00:06:59.523
Through our roles,
we speak to the audience's emotions!

00:06:59.607 --> 00:07:03.694
If my private life is shown too…

00:07:04.654 --> 00:07:05.988
It just takes away from it.

00:07:07.865 --> 00:07:10.284
That's exactly
why I don't do social media.

00:07:10.368 --> 00:07:13.746
Koji Yakusho, my idol,
doesn't use it either. He's so mysterious.

00:07:13.829 --> 00:07:15.957
Well, of course,
Koji Yakusho wouldn't use it.

00:07:16.666 --> 00:07:17.875
Konta.

00:07:17.959 --> 00:07:19.544
-Yeah?
-I'm sorry.

00:07:20.336 --> 00:07:22.046
As your younger sister,

00:07:22.713 --> 00:07:24.966
I'm just going to go ahead and say it.

00:07:25.049 --> 00:07:26.133
What?

00:07:27.385 --> 00:07:30.638
You can't afford
to have such picky standards!

00:07:30.721 --> 00:07:31.764
Whoa.

00:07:31.847 --> 00:07:37.436
Building your recognition and getting work
is the most important thing, isn't it?

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:41.399
Right? Literally nobody knows
you even exist right now.

00:07:41.482 --> 00:07:43.317
-Exist?
-Yeah. And!

00:07:43.401 --> 00:07:47.446
You're "mysterious" in the sense
that you don't even exist in the industry.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:48.406
Mysterious?

00:07:48.489 --> 00:07:51.993
Listen! You need to let people know
who Konta Hoshino even is!

00:07:52.076 --> 00:07:54.704
To that end,
refusing jobs is out of the question!

00:07:55.913 --> 00:07:57.665
Is that so?

00:07:57.748 --> 00:07:59.000
Yes, it is.

00:08:06.799 --> 00:08:07.967
Then…

00:08:09.594 --> 00:08:10.469
I'll do it.

00:08:10.553 --> 00:08:11.804
What did you say?

00:08:13.681 --> 00:08:16.183
This Document Memoreal job…

00:08:18.644 --> 00:08:20.021
I guess I'll take it!

00:08:33.117 --> 00:08:35.620
Sorry for making you help out
with the cleaning.

00:08:35.703 --> 00:08:38.414
It's fine. Let's make it
look nice for the shoot.

00:08:38.497 --> 00:08:39.665
Thanks.

00:08:42.585 --> 00:08:43.878
Konta, did you not sleep?

00:08:43.961 --> 00:08:46.797
As a reference for today's show,

00:08:46.881 --> 00:08:49.967
I was binge-watching documentaries
on famous actors.

00:08:50.051 --> 00:08:51.135
I see.

00:08:51.218 --> 00:08:53.262
That doesn't sound good.

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:01.729
Hup.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:07.526
Let me carry that.

00:09:08.152 --> 00:09:09.320
Mr. Nishigami.

00:09:10.321 --> 00:09:11.697
Thank you very much.

00:09:13.032 --> 00:09:14.867
Cleaning the villa?

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:16.369
Oh, yes.

00:09:16.452 --> 00:09:19.163
My brother is going to be
in a day-in-the-life feature.

00:09:19.246 --> 00:09:20.331
Day-in-the-life?

00:09:20.414 --> 00:09:23.250
So we have to clean up the villa.

00:09:23.334 --> 00:09:27.088
So, for this show, is someone coming over?

00:09:27.588 --> 00:09:30.966
Just the director.
Seems he is coming alone with a camera.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:35.346
Oh, but we'll make sure
not to cause you any inconvenience.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:39.725
How long will they be staying?

00:09:39.809 --> 00:09:42.395
I heard it will be about three days.

00:09:43.354 --> 00:09:46.107
Still, I'm very worried.

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:47.483
I see.

00:09:48.859 --> 00:09:52.405
But I'm happy for Mr. Konta.

00:09:59.537 --> 00:10:03.499
Wow, it's so clean now!
Rinrin, Tsumugi, thank you.

00:10:03.582 --> 00:10:04.709
You're welcome.

00:10:04.792 --> 00:10:06.293
Hey!

00:10:07.712 --> 00:10:10.423
What do you think about my clothes?

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:13.884
Huh? Do you plan
to be on the show like that?

00:10:13.968 --> 00:10:14.927
Well, yeah.

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:16.470
Absolutely don't do that!

00:10:16.554 --> 00:10:20.558
Really? Wait, don't I look sharp in this?

00:10:22.685 --> 00:10:23.644
You're so uncool.

00:10:23.728 --> 00:10:25.646
Promise me you won't wear that outfit.

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:28.691
Oh, really?
I think it looks awesome, though.

00:10:31.527 --> 00:10:34.280
All right!
To get ready for the shoot tomorrow,

00:10:34.363 --> 00:10:37.366
Tetsuro, could you give my face
a massage to slim it down?

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:39.326
I've never done anything like that before.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:42.288
It's fine. Just search,
"Slimming face massage,"

00:10:42.371 --> 00:10:44.248
"How to do," and you'll get it.

00:10:44.331 --> 00:10:46.250
-Do it! Let's go.
-Okay, I'll look it up.

00:10:46.333 --> 00:10:49.086
Don't leave me behind.
Hey, don't leave the star behind!

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:51.338
Which way am I supposed to go? Straight?

00:10:51.422 --> 00:10:53.132
Watch out, there's a step.

00:10:53.215 --> 00:10:56.385
Why are you saying that yourself?
Hey, there's a huge step again.

00:10:56.469 --> 00:10:58.262
Konta is really getting cocky.

00:10:58.345 --> 00:11:00.931
Just yesterday, he was wondering
whether he should accept it.

00:11:01.015 --> 00:11:01.849
Yeah.

00:11:01.932 --> 00:11:06.437
He definitely thinks he'll go viral
and become popular after the show.

00:11:07.062 --> 00:11:08.981
I wonder if things
will really go that well.

00:11:14.153 --> 00:11:15.362
Good morning.

00:11:15.446 --> 00:11:17.448
Hello.

00:11:18.115 --> 00:11:20.826
Good morning.
I'm Torihara from Document Memoreal.

00:11:22.286 --> 00:11:24.330
I'm the actor, Konta… Wait.

00:11:25.539 --> 00:11:27.583
I'm the actor…

00:11:27.666 --> 00:11:29.502
Konta Hoshino.

00:11:29.585 --> 00:11:30.836
Thank you very much.

00:11:33.422 --> 00:11:36.300
This is the schedule we have planned.

00:11:40.429 --> 00:11:42.806
Has the narrator been decided yet?

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:44.433
Oh, not yet.

00:11:44.517 --> 00:11:47.186
Then please get Koji Yakusho.

00:11:47.937 --> 00:11:50.523
No, I don't think we can…

00:11:50.606 --> 00:11:52.650
Just ask him, just in case.

00:11:52.733 --> 00:11:56.612
Narration is very important
for a documentary. Get someone good!

00:11:57.196 --> 00:12:00.324
For now, shall we start shooting
the villa's exterior?

00:12:00.407 --> 00:12:01.617
-All right.
-Let's do it.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:03.202
Midori, guide him.

00:12:03.285 --> 00:12:05.079
Okay. This way.

00:12:05.162 --> 00:12:06.580
Thank you very much.

00:12:08.207 --> 00:12:09.875
Are you a family member?

00:12:09.959 --> 00:12:11.585
Well, he's my older brother.

00:12:11.669 --> 00:12:12.920
-Oh, I see.
-Yeah.

00:12:13.003 --> 00:12:14.838
I would like to interview you later.

00:12:18.259 --> 00:12:21.387
Hello? Mr. Torihara is already here.

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:22.972
Oh, sorry.

00:12:23.055 --> 00:12:26.141
I'm at a different set now,
I don't have time to head over there.

00:12:26.225 --> 00:12:28.018
You'll be fine on your own, right?

00:12:28.102 --> 00:12:30.479
What? Seriously?

00:12:30.563 --> 00:12:33.357
How can I look professional
if my manager isn't here?

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:35.109
Come on!

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:39.822
What should I do? A manager…

00:12:40.447 --> 00:12:43.576
This is a really magnificent villa.

00:12:44.118 --> 00:12:46.328
It's actually my grandmother's place.

00:12:47.454 --> 00:12:51.083
Mr. Torihara,
please take good care of my brother.

00:12:51.166 --> 00:12:52.084
What?

00:12:52.167 --> 00:12:55.337
To be honest, he is an idiot,

00:12:55.421 --> 00:12:59.508
but he works really hard
to get acting jobs.

00:12:59.592 --> 00:13:01.135
Leave it to me.

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:04.346
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:07.016
Nice to meet you.

00:13:07.099 --> 00:13:09.310
Why those outfits and make-up?

00:13:09.393 --> 00:13:10.978
We thought we might be on camera too.

00:13:11.061 --> 00:13:13.564
Men may see us and think,
"Who is that girl?"

00:13:13.647 --> 00:13:15.232
And contact us!

00:13:15.316 --> 00:13:16.859
-That sounds good.
-Good?

00:13:16.942 --> 00:13:20.070
What exactly are you expecting
from my brother's show?

00:13:20.154 --> 00:13:21.447
It's a possibility.

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:22.948
Hello.

00:13:23.032 --> 00:13:26.118
-Nice to meet you.
-This is my manager.

00:13:26.201 --> 00:13:27.077
-What?
-Konta…

00:13:27.161 --> 00:13:28.287
Just play along.

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:31.624
Hello, I am Director Torihara.

00:13:32.416 --> 00:13:35.085
I am Konta Hoshino's manager.

00:13:35.169 --> 00:13:36.503
-Well then, everyone…
-Sorry.

00:13:36.587 --> 00:13:38.797
I look forward to working with you all!

00:13:38.881 --> 00:13:40.215
The pleasure is ours!

00:13:40.299 --> 00:13:41.216
Thank you.

00:13:50.934 --> 00:13:55.314
That villa attracts
one human after another.

00:14:04.281 --> 00:14:09.119
I could never have imagined
you were the mastermind all along.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:13.749
Yes, that's a wrap for this cut.

00:14:13.832 --> 00:14:16.251
Wow, that was wonderful.

00:14:16.335 --> 00:14:18.504
May I ask a few questions?

00:14:18.587 --> 00:14:21.757
I truly think you are
a one-of-a-kind actor, Konta.

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:23.050
One-of-a-kind, yes.

00:14:23.133 --> 00:14:25.594
Are there any actors
you take inspiration from?

00:14:25.678 --> 00:14:27.054
Well…

00:14:27.137 --> 00:14:28.305
DiCaprio, I suppose.

00:14:28.389 --> 00:14:29.598
DiCap--

00:14:29.682 --> 00:14:32.434
I feel a sort of connection with him.

00:14:32.518 --> 00:14:36.397
He has the same eyes as me.

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:38.691
T-The same eyes?

00:14:38.774 --> 00:14:41.110
Oh, yes. The same eyes.

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:44.697
Well, our facial features
are quite similar too.

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:45.990
Of course,

00:14:46.073 --> 00:14:50.202
he is a Hollywood superstar,
but I plan on catching up to him.

00:14:50.285 --> 00:14:53.664
Or rather, overtaking him,
so you could say he's my rival?

00:14:54.415 --> 00:14:56.375
Something like a rival, I guess.

00:14:57.418 --> 00:15:00.295
Interesting. May I ask one more question?

00:15:00.379 --> 00:15:02.381
Are you okay? Please drink some water.

00:15:02.464 --> 00:15:05.342
My throat is dry.
Your questions are coming too fast.

00:15:05.426 --> 00:15:06.677
Sorry, I got carried away.

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:09.847
Is there anything you try
to be mindful of when acting?

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:11.682
-Oh, actors…
-Yes.

00:15:11.765 --> 00:15:16.395
When we act,
we live out the lives of many people.

00:15:16.478 --> 00:15:20.399
But, of course, I am also a person,
and I have a life of my own.

00:15:20.482 --> 00:15:23.944
So, in the moments
when I live another person's life,

00:15:24.028 --> 00:15:25.612
I sort of kill my own self.

00:15:25.696 --> 00:15:28.073
Or rather, it's like… How should I put it…

00:15:28.741 --> 00:15:29.867
How should I put it…

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:32.578
-How do you put it?
-How should I put it…

00:15:38.042 --> 00:15:39.209
Bloodlust…

00:15:40.169 --> 00:15:41.211
Who goes there?

00:15:46.633 --> 00:15:48.343
What? Who goes there?

00:16:00.022 --> 00:16:01.565
Come here!

00:16:02.232 --> 00:16:04.735
You come here! Come!

00:16:08.322 --> 00:16:10.032
Is he really going to be okay?

00:16:10.115 --> 00:16:11.241
I don't know.

00:16:11.325 --> 00:16:13.786
He might be getting a little carried away.

00:16:35.599 --> 00:16:37.851
For us actors,
our bodies are our greatest asset.

00:16:37.935 --> 00:16:38.936
You're amazing.

00:16:39.019 --> 00:16:40.854
Oh, that's great.

00:16:40.938 --> 00:16:43.524
It would be great
if this really makes Konta successful.

00:16:43.607 --> 00:16:47.027
It's like my brother has completely
changed since the show started.

00:16:47.111 --> 00:16:48.987
I don't want people to find out I'm poor!

00:16:49.071 --> 00:16:50.155
It's actually good!

00:16:50.864 --> 00:16:51.907
What a handsome man.

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:53.617
Please don't film that man.

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:55.744
Acting is my true calling.

00:16:55.828 --> 00:16:58.038
I was born to act.

00:16:58.122 --> 00:16:59.832
You are an example for all actors.

00:16:59.915 --> 00:17:02.626
If we inflate his ego more,
we can film something way funnier.

00:17:02.709 --> 00:17:04.795
That's what the viewers are looking for.

00:17:04.878 --> 00:17:07.714
Everyone is supporting me,
so I want to get on top,

00:17:07.798 --> 00:17:09.466
for their sake.

00:17:10.676 --> 00:17:11.635
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.